msgid "Tools"
msgstr "Espleches"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:495
#, no-c-format
msgid "Molecular Editor"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:496
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Molecular Editor allows you to view and edit molecules using <ulink url="
"\"http://avogadro.openmolecules.net/wiki/Main_Page\">Avogadro</ulink> "
"libraries."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:499
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using control panel on the left you can change the view parameters, edit "
"molecule, or measure molecules. There are three tabs on this panel: "
"<guilabel>Display</guilabel>, <guilabel>Edit</guilabel>, and "
"<guilabel>Measure</guilabel>. The buttons along the bottom of the window can "
"be used to <guibutton>Save molecule</guibutton>, <guibutton>Download New "
"Molecules</guibutton>, <guibutton>Load Molecule</guibutton>, and "
"<guibutton>Close</guibutton> the window. The downloaded from kde-apps data "
"will be saved in <filename class=\"directory\">$KDEHOME/share/apps/kalzium/"
"molecules</filename>, they should be renamed to "
"<filename><replaceable>molecule_name</replaceable>.cml</filename> manually. "
"<envar>$KDEHOME</envar> is usually a hidden folder in your Home folder "
"called <filename class=\"directory\">.kde</filename> or <filename class="
"\"directory\">.kde4</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:506
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Statistics</guilabel> pane shows name (if available), formula, and "
"weight of the molecule."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:509
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Display</guilabel> tab can be used to change "
"<guilabel>Quality</guilabel> of the image (<guimenuitem>Low</guimenuitem>, "
"<guimenuitem>Medium</guimenuitem>, or <guimenuitem>High</guimenuitem>, can "
"be useful on low-end system), <guilabel>Style</guilabel> (can be "
"<guimenuitem>Balls and sticks</guimenuitem>, <guimenuitem>Sticks</"
"guimenuitem>, <guimenuitem>Van der Waals</guimenuitem>, or "
"<guimenuitem>Wireframe</guimenuitem>), <guilabel>2nd Style</guilabel> (can "
"be <guimenuitem>None</guimenuitem>, <guimenuitem>Ribbon</guimenuitem>, "
"<guimenuitem>Ring</guimenuitem>, or <guimenuitem>Molecular Orbital</"
"guimenuitem>), and <guilabel>Labels</guilabel> (can be <guimenuitem>None</"
"guimenuitem>, <guimenuitem>Atom Numbers</guimenuitem>, <guimenuitem>Element "
"Names</guimenuitem>, or <guimenuitem>Element Symbols</guimenuitem>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:512
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Edit</guilabel> tab is aimed to edit molecule. You can add "
"elements by choosing them in <guilabel>Elements</guilabel> drop-down list "
"and clicking with &LMB; on view panel. The molecule can be optimized by "
"clicking <guibutton>Optimize</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:515
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Measure</guilabel> tab can be used to measure distances and "
"angles in the molecule. To make the measurement use the instructions shown "
"on the tab."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:518
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the right of the <guilabel>Molecular Editor</guilabel> window the "
"molecule will be shown. Use &LMB; to rotate molecule, &RMB; to move it, and "
"&MMB; to zoom."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:527
#, no-c-format
msgid "the <quote>Molecular Editor</quote>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:533
#, no-c-format
msgid "Isotope Table"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:534
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guimenuitem>Isotope Table...</guimenuitem> shows you the isotopes of "
"the elements."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:537
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are different kinds of isotopes, some are stable, some are not. The "
"unstable isotopes can decay as alpha-rays are two different beta-rays. These "
"differences are encoded by using different colors."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:546
#, no-c-format
msgid "the <quote>Isotope Table</quote> window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:548
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kalzium; can display the isotopes of a range of elements"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:554
#, no-c-format
msgid "Plot Data"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:555
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guimenuitem>Plot Data...</guimenuitem> dialog allows you to plot some "
"information about elements. The X-axis represents a range of elements (from "
"one number to a higher number). You set this range using the <guilabel>First "
"Element</guilabel> and <guilabel>Last Element</guilabel> fields on the "
"dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:564
#, no-c-format
msgid "the <quote>Plot Data</quote> Dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:566
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kalzium; can plot some data about a range of elements."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:572
#, no-c-format
msgid "Perform Calculation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:573
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Perform Calculation</guilabel> is the &kalzium; calculator. "
"This calculator contains a variety of calculators for different tasks "
"performing different calculations."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:576
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can find the following calculators in &kalzium;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:581
#, no-c-format
msgid "Molecular mass calculator"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:583
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This calculator helps you calculate the molecular masses of different "
"molecules."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:586
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can specify short form of the molecule names add more such aliases."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:595
#, no-c-format
msgid "the <quote>Molecular mass calculator</quote> dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:597
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kalzium; calculates molecular mass of phenol."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:604
#, no-c-format
msgid "Concentrations calculator"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:606
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can calculate quantities which include"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:611
#, no-c-format
msgid "Amount of substance"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:616
#, no-c-format
msgid "Volume of solvent"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:621
#, no-c-format
msgid "Concentration of substance"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:626
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are a wide range of units to choose from and different methods to "
"specify quantities."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:635
#, no-c-format
msgid "the <quote>Concentrations calculator</quote> dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:637
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kalzium; calculates solution parameters."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:644
#, no-c-format
msgid "Nuclear calculator"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:646
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This calculator makes use of the nuclear data available in &kalzium; to "
"predict the expected masses of a material after time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:655
#, no-c-format
msgid "the <quote>Nuclear calculator</quote> dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:657
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kalzium; calculates parameters of uranium decay."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:664
#, no-c-format
msgid "Gas calculator"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:666
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This calculator can calculate the values of Temperature, pressure, volume, "
"amount of gas etc. for various ideal as well as non-ideal gases."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:675
#, no-c-format
msgid "the <quote>Gas calculator</quote> dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:677
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kalzium; calculates gas parameters."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: index.docbook:684
#, no-c-format
msgid "Titration calculator"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:686
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This calculator tries to find out the equivalence point of a pH-meter "
"followed titration best fitting it with an hyperbolic tangent. You can also "
"let it solve an equilibrium system of equations and see how the "
"concentration of a species changes in function of another one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:689
#, no-c-format
msgid "There are two tabs on the calculator page, namely:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:694
#, no-c-format
msgid "Experimental Values"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:696
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use this calculator to draw the plot of your experimental data "
"obtained during a titration and find out the volume of equivalence. It's "
"strongly recommended to insert a even number of points, because of the best "
"fit algorithm, sorted by volume (the X axis value)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:702
#, no-c-format
msgid "Theoretical Equations"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:704
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can fill the table with the equations you have previously obtained "
"for the chemical equilibrium."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:707
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For example, if you have this reaction <emphasis>A + B -> C + D</emphasis> "
"then you will have the equation <emphasis>K=(C*D)/(A*B)</emphasis> so you "
"must write <userinput>K</userinput> in the <guilabel>Parameter</guilabel> "
"column and <userinput>(C*D)/(A*B)</userinput> in the <guilabel>Value</"
"guilabel> column. If you want to assign a known value to a parameter you can "
"simply write the numeric value in the <guilabel>Value</guilabel> field."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:710
#, no-c-format
msgid "For example, you can use the system"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:714
#, no-c-format
msgid "A=(C*D)/(B*K)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:717
#, no-c-format
msgid "K=10^-3"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:720
#, no-c-format
msgid "C=OH"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:723
#, no-c-format
msgid "OH=(10^-14)/H"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:726
#, no-c-format
msgid "H=10^-4"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:729
#, no-c-format
msgid "B=6*(10^-2)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:731
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Then you have to write <userinput>D</userinput> as <guilabel>X axis</"
"guilabel> and <userinput>A</userinput> as <guilabel>Y axis</guilabel>: so "
"you will find out how the concentration of A changes as a function of D "
"concentration."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:735
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Please don't use parenthesis for exponents: <userinput>10^-3</userinput> is "
"correct, while <userinput>10^(-3)</userinput> is wrong."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:742
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The results can be visualized by pressing <guibutton>Draw Plot</guibutton> "
"button. The plot shows in red the curve that comes from theoretical "
"equations, in blue the experimental points, and in green the approximated "
"curve for experimental points. You can save the plot as SVG image."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:751
#, no-c-format
msgid "the <quote>Titration calculator</quote> dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:753
#, no-c-format
msgid "Predefined example of titration results."
msgstr ""

